{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["Now the manna was as coriander seed — and its appearance as the appearance of bdellium — meaning: it appeared hard and dry, and therefore they would say: ״ונפשנו יבשה״ — like a person who eats dry grains of wheat. If so, why did the anger of the Holy One, blessed be He, burn as stated before us? And now Scripture explains the reason for the burning anger, for — when they ground it in mills or crushed it in a mortar — then — ״והיה טעמו כטעם לשד השמן״ — then its taste changed from what it was at first, sweet — ״כצפיחית בדבש״ — like olives and nuts before grinding; but after grinding or crushing in a mortar, then ״והיה טעמו״ — its taste now became like the richness of oil and fat meat, like olive oil and nut oil after grinding, whose taste has changed. And therefore ״וישמע ה׳״ — ״ויחר אפו״ — because when they want to grind it, it becomes like oil, and their food is not dry. Here it is written: ״והיה טעמו״ — that its first taste changes; but in the section of Beshalaḥ it is written: ״וטעמו כצפיחית בדבש״ — for that is its taste before it takes on the taste of oil."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:49:59.152225808Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}